  "notes": "The third of the three prayers before Communion. Like the second, it carries no rubric segment: the witnesses print one rubric for all three, and it stands at the head of ordinarium.qui-dixisti. QUOD at w007 is neuter and picks up Córporis, not the feminine Percéptio that governs the sentence — the relative crosses over its nearer noun to reach the right one. PERCIPIÉNDAM at w033 is a gerundive, written as SCHEMA.md requires: a future passive participle, mood part, tense fut, voice pass, with the case, number and gender of medélam. PROSIT at w023 is prosum, a compound of sum, so it carries no conjugation. JUDÍCIUM at w016 is one of the ju- words the Whitaker's port does not carry; its provenance names Collatinus alone, as the corpus already records for judicáre, júbeas and justum.",
